            "subject": "LU-21218 ksocklnd: accept connects while own connect is stuck"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Jinshan Xiong",
          "email": "jinshanx@google.com",
          "date": "2026-11-14 20:32:34.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Jinshan Xiong",
          "email": "jinshanx@google.com",
          "date": "2026-11-17 05:45:24.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21219 ksocklnd: complete txs with an errno after retry cap",
        "message": "LU-21219 ksocklnd: complete txs with an errno after retry cap\n\nAfter SOCKNAL_MAX_RETRIES connection attempts that the peer refused\nas \"connection race resolution\" or \"duplicate\", ksocknal_connect()\ngives up with \"goto failed\" while rc still holds the positive retry\ncode from ksocknal_create_conn() (e.g. EALREADY).  The blocked txs are\nthen completed with a positive status, which lnet_ping() reports as\nthe number of NIDs in the reply.  lnet_ping_show_dump() walks that\nmany entries of an empty list and crashes:\n\n  ping event (5 114)\n  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000001\n  RIP: lnet_ping_show_dump+0x3dc\n\nNegate rc before failing, as ksocknal_create_conn() already does for\nits own zombie txs, so the txs are completed with a negative errno.\nAlso reset the retry count whenever the cap is reached, whether we\nsettle for the connections we have or give up.  Otherwise the next\nksocknal_connect() for the conn_cb hits the cap at its first refusal\nand drops the queued txs at once, and can reach the cap with no\nrefusal at all and rc == 0.  Also make lnet_ping() return only a\nnegative event status when no reply arrived, since its callers take\nany value >= 0 as a NID count.\n\nReproduced by sanity-lnet test_239 without the previous patch (the\nlower NID's connects are rejected while the peer's own connect is\nstuck): the node crashed in 3 of 3 runs.  With the sign fix the test\nfails cleanly with -EALREADY instead.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 02caf7170762 (\"LU-17258 socklnd: stop connecting on too many retries\")\nFixes: d4c52652c357 (\"LU-19225 socklnd: cap the number of retries\")\nSigned-off-by: Jinshan Xiong <jinshanx@google.com>\nAssisted-by: Jetski:gemini-4-argon\nChange-Id: I786bb284d7aef84801b83d3a99d162bf0da3fbaf\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
